@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` is exported from `src/index.ts` and resolves an
+[RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901.html) JSON Pointer string against a parsed JSON
+document. An empty pointer returns the document itself; `/items/0` selects the first item of an
+`items` array. Within member names, use `~0` for `~` and `~1` for `/`.
+
+Invalid syntax and unresolved references throw an error, including `-` and out-of-range indices
+when accessing arrays. Pass plain pointer strings, not URI fragments such as `#/items/0`.
+Resolution does not mutate the document and returns selected objects and arrays by reference.
+
+Run `npm test` with Node.js 22.18 or newer.
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
